{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And he laid his hands, etc. and he charged him.</b> Meaning, an expression of command (tzavta), for he illuminated in him the radiance of the soul, as I explained above regarding what is written ״וְסָמַכְתָּ״. According to this, examine precisely what it says: <b>as HaShem spoke by the hand of Moses</b> — for this statement has no apparent meaning: is this speech then a matter grasped by the hand? Rather, the meaning is that HaShem spoke — that the efflux of radiance would be by the hand of Moses to Joshua. It further alludes to royalty (kingly authority), on the path of the Sages, whose memory is for blessing: 'There is no צו but royalty' (I Samuel 13:14), as it is written ״וַיְצַוֵּנִי ה׳ לְנָגִיד״. Examine precisely as well what it says: as HaShem spoke by the hand of Moses — meaning that the royalty — HaShem spoke that it would be by the hand of Moses, in place of the anointing oil."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:15:42.232748260Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}